<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="086" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Rate card and rate join the secure family; timekeeper rows get their own owner (uac-r2 review item 5)</title>
    <phase>3 Rules (WP3) — rule-set scope (D-171, D-172, D-141), wave W3-10</phase>
    <gate>081 and 085 done; owner OK for the live refusal probes and the two -Apply runs on dev</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Record ownership on Secure records (a Secure-scoped import is refused today; a later Secure is never followed), uac-r2's lineage, resolver, role, census and depth-assertion files, and live role and schema writes on dev: tenant-isolation code.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-relevant ownership change across uac-r2-owned files with a binding review, mirroring 081's secure-family change for a second pair of tables.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits the same uac-r2 files and shared guards as 081 (SecureChildLineage.cs, RecordOwnershipResolver.cs, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, RecordCreatorPerson.cs, scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1, SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests) and RateCardImportService.cs after 085. Run /conflict-check before the PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>081, 085</deps>
    <tags>bff, security, tenant-isolation, testing, rules</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Put sprk_ratecard and sprk_ratecardrate in the secure family in ONE change, as 081 does for sprk_ruleset (notes/rule-set-scope-design.md section 5.4): lineage entries, sprk_ratecard in OwnershipParentEntities, role rows with live refusal probes applied before the BFF deploy, sprk_createdbyperson on both, census ChildTables / Routed entries / PersonBearingWriters, and the NFR-05 depth check on both. In RateCardImportService, take each row's owner parents from its own lookups (card → core record, rate → card) and give new firm-level timekeeper rows their own owner (no parents), never the matter's.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in IRecordOwnershipResolver, SecureChildReconciler, the uac-r2 secure-family guards and the rate card import (078).</role>

  <goal>A rate card import scoped to a Secure matter succeeds, its card and rates owned by the Secure team; making a matter Secure later re-owns its card and rates through the reconciler (and Unsecure moves them back); new timekeeper rows are owned by the caller's business-unit team whatever the card's scope; SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, the census and the creator-person agreement test pass with both tables; the NFR-05 run reports no non-admin role reaching the Secure business unit on either table.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design note section 5.4 and section 12 (uac-r2 review item 5). Decisions: D-120 (a card is deleted with its record), D-137 / ontology D-172 (Q8 direct inheritance is a read rule), D-141. The gap (at 3e11367468): RateCardImportService.ImportAsync (:152) resolves one owner from the core record (:200-211) and applies it to the timekeeper rows (:287), the card (:314) and the rates (:343), and passes it to the workbook document (:237); neither sprk_ratecard nor sprk_ratecardrate is in SecureChildLineage, config/secure-record-owner-role.json or the census (RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests has no RateCardImportService entry). Entity sets: sprk_ratecards, sprk_ratecardrates (docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md:12, :35). sprk_ratecardrate.sprk_ratecard is parental (cascade assign). Spaarke Basic User and Core User hold prvReadsprk_ratecard and prvReadsprk_ratecardrate at Deep (SpaarkeMaster Roles :523-524, :596-597). The 081 change is the reference for every file touched.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/RateCardImportService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureChildLineage.cs (uac-r2)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/RecordOwnershipResolver.cs (OwnershipParentEntities only; uac-r2)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/RecordCreatorPerson.cs (StampedChildTables; uac-r2)</file>
      <file role="modify">scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 ($Tables and solution map; uac-r2)</file>
      <file role="modify">config/secure-record-owner-role.json (two rows with probe evidence; uac-r2)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Dataverse/SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs (GuardedPrivileges; uac-r2)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/SecureBuRoleDepthAssertionTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/SecureFamilyConsistencyTests.cs (only if its expectations are literal)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/domain/Access/SecureChildLineageTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Finance/RateCardImportServiceTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Access/SecureChildReconcilerRateCardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="read">the 081 diff and notes/081-ruleset-scope-service.md (the reference change)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="081" status="pending">The secure-family change for sprk_ruleset (same files; this task follows its shape)</dependency>
      <dependency task="085" status="pending">RateCardImportService writes sprk_scope (same file)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 5, design note 5.4">ONE change carries every part: SecureChildLineage T("sprk_ratecard", "sprk_ratecards", ("sprk_matter", Matter), ("sprk_project", Project), ("sprk_workassignment", WorkAssignment)) and T("sprk_ratecardrate", "sprk_ratecardrates", ("sprk_ratecard", "sprk_ratecard")); "sprk_ratecard" in OwnershipParentEntities (the parent of its rates; sprk_ratecardrate is a lineage child only); role rows for both (kind child, Read, Basic, reason, verbatim probe evidence); both in RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1; census ChildTables, Routed entries for the RateCardImportService card and rate creates, and a PersonBearingWriters entry ("RateCardImportService.cs", "ImportAsync", the admin who imported); GuardedPrivileges for both tables.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 4 (same rule as 081)">Each row's owner parents come from its own lookups through RecordOwnershipContext.ParentsOf(row): the card from its core lookup (none for a Firm card), each rate from its sprk_ratecard. ResolveOwnerAsync(ForParents(..., caller) with { RequestedBy = caller }). A refusal writes nothing (the existing OwnerRefused outcome).</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 5 (timekeepers)">New sprk_timekeeper rows are firm-level: their owner is a NO-PARENT resolution (the caller's business-unit team, RequestedBy = caller), resolved once per import and never the card's owner, whatever the card's scope. Existing roster rows the import reuses are not touched. sprk_timekeeper does not join the secure family.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 1 (live part, as 081)">Live refusal probes on dev, one per table, before the privileges are added (verbatim 0x80040299 into the evidence); then Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -WhatIf / -Apply / -Verify and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 dry run / -Apply / -Verify, each with the owner's OK. Both MUST be applied before any BFF carrying this code is deployed (079 re-verifies).</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 1 (NFR-05)">The depth check covers sprk_ratecard and sprk_ratecardrate for every non-admin role; record the live NFR-05 result on dev.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-120, D-141">No delete code and no delete-Restrict: uac-r2's delete job already deletes a card scoped to the record (+ its rates). Q8 is unchanged: a matter's card judges its direct children's invoices app-only; joining the secure family changes who can READ the card, not which invoices it judges.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">BFF hygiene: no new service or registration; publish-size delta; no package; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/notes/rule-set-scope-design.md (sections 3.5, 5.1, 5.4, 12)</file>
      <file>projects/ebilling-r1/tasks/081-ruleset-scope-service-ownership.poml</file>
      <file>docs/data-model/sprk_ratecard.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="The secure-family change for one table" location="081's diff (SecureChildLineage, OwnershipParentEntities, role JSON, StampedChildTables, census, GuardedPrivileges)">Copy its shape for two tables.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Reconciler test fixture" location="tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Access/SecureChildReconcilerGateDecisionRecordTests.cs, TestInfrastructure/SecureChildReconcilerFixtures.cs">Card and rate re-owned on secure and on unsecure.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">git merge-base --is-ancestor 3e11367468 HEAD; confirm 081 and 085 are merged; read notes/081-ruleset-scope-service.md.</step>
    <step order="1">RateCardImportService: parents from each row's own lookups; the timekeeper owner as a separate no-parent resolution; tests (Secure-scoped import, Firm import, timekeeper owner under a Secure-scoped import, refusal writes nothing).</step>
    <step order="2">Secure family in one change: lineage, OwnershipParentEntities, StampedChildTables + script, role rows, census, GuardedPrivileges; SecureChildLineageTests, SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, the reconciler test (card and rates re-owned on secure and unsecure).</step>
    <step order="3">The workbook document (sprk_document, created unlinked with the card's owner at :237): agree its owner with uac-r2 (escalation); implement only what they agree.</step>
    <step order="4">With the owner's OK: the probes, both -Apply runs with -Verify, the live NFR-05 run. Notices to uac-r2 before and after.</step>
    <step order="5">dotnet build; dotnet test (unit, ArchTests, the data-mutation agreement test); publish-size delta; /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="6">Review: uac-r2. Record it.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/086-ratecard-secure-family.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any part of the secure-family change cannot land in the same PR as the others, STOP (a subset fails SecureFamilyConsistencyTests or the census).</trigger>
    <trigger>If a probe's create SUCCEEDS, delete the probe row, record it and STOP; ask uac-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the live NFR-05 run reports a non-admin role whose Read on sprk_ratecard or sprk_ratecardrate reaches the Secure business unit, STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required.</trigger>
    <trigger>The workbook document's owner: if uac-r2 does not agree a rule (the card's owner with a filing link, or a no-parent owner like the timekeepers), leave its current behaviour, record it as a deferred issue with /project-defer-issue-tracking, and report it; do not invent a lookup.</trigger>
    <trigger>If routing needs a resolver change beyond adding sprk_ratecard to OwnershipParentEntities, STOP and ask uac-r2.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The cards, rates and import exist (017, 078); the secure-family lists and guards exist and already take sprk_ruleset (081); the resolver already routes the card's owner. Grep finds sprk_ratecard in none of SecureChildLineage, the role JSON, StampedChildTables or the census.</existing>
    <extension>Only existing lists, guards and the import are extended; no new service, registration, table or endpoint. Two new list entries per guard plus one reconciler test file.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A rate card import scoped to a Secure matter is refused by Dataverse (0x80040299); a card on a matter made Secure later stays readable outside the wall; and a Secure matter's import hides new firm timekeepers from the firm's ordinary readers.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build, test</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1, Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 (owner OK)</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-mcp">probes (owner OK), role and metadata reads</tool>
    <tool name="conflict-check">before the PR</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">RateCardImportService.cs, SecureChildLineage.cs, RecordOwnershipResolver.cs, RecordCreatorPerson.cs, SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs, config/secure-record-owner-role.json, scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1</output>
    <output type="test">the test files listed in relevant-files</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/086-ratecard-secure-family.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An import scoped to a Secure matter resolves the Secure team as owner of the card and every rate, and creates them (unit test with the resolver; the live probe shows the role row is what makes Dataverse accept it).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Owner parents: the card passes exactly [core record] (none for a Firm card); each rate passes exactly [the card] (negative: never [core record]).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Timekeepers: under a Secure-scoped import a new timekeeper row is owned by the caller's business-unit team (no parents), not the Secure team (negative); a reused roster row is not written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The reconciler test re-owns a matter's card and its rates when the matter is made Secure, and moves them back on Unsecure; a Firm card (no lookup) is never reached (negative).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, EveryChildTableTheServerCreatesCarriesTheCreatorPersonColumn, EveryAppCreateWriterThatActsForAPersonNamesThem, EveryRoutedEntryRoutesThroughTheResolver and ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchemaAgreementTests pass with both tables; removing either table from the role JSON fails SecureFamilyConsistencyTests (seeding proof).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GuardedPrivileges covers both tables; the live NFR-05 run on dev is recorded with no finding on them.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Notes record both probes' verbatim refusals, the -Apply / -Verify outputs, the owner's OK with dates, and uac-r2's answer on the workbook document.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta recorded; no package; no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check run.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>A task of its own (design note 5.4): 085 is a resolver change that runs beside 083 (p-safe true); this one edits uac-r2's shared files after 081, needs live probes and uac-r2's review, and follows 085 on RateCardImportService.cs. Two adversarial passes (tenant-isolation).</notes>

